<title>USA: Worldtalk names Harguindeguy CEO.</title>
<headline>Worldtalk names Harguindeguy CEO.</headline>
<dateline>SANTA CLARA, Calif. 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>WorldTalk Corp said on Thursday company founder Mark Jung had resigned and it promoted president and chief operating officer Bernard Harguindeguy, 39, to the additional post of chief executive.</p>
<p>Jung would continue to serve a consultant to the Worldtalk board and senior management, the company said.</p>
<p>Worldtalk provides directory-based messaging and security software solutions.</p>
<p>&quot;I am pleased with this transaction, after having recruited Bernard Harguindeguy to Worldtalk...,&quot; Jung said.</p>
<p>((New York newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
